.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt WINDOW-SCREENSHOT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm window-screenshot
.Nd grab the focused window to a PNG
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl feedback
.Op Ar window-id
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
grabs one window with
.Xr gm 1
.Cm import
and writes a PNG.
.Ar window-id
is an X id, decimal or hex.
When it is omitted, the focused window is used.
.Pp
The file is
.Pa ~/screenshot- Ns Ar YYYY.MM.DD-HH.MM.SS Ns Pa .png .
.Pa ~/screenshot-latest.png
is a symbolic link to it.
The path is printed.
.Pp
.Fl Fl feedback
shows the file name through
.Xr bosd 1 ,
the same green caption as
.Xr desktop-screenshot 1 .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "DISPLAY"
.It Ev DISPLAY
X server.
The default is
.Pa :0 .
.It Ev HOME
Directory of the grab.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/screenshot-YYYY.MM.DD-HH.MM.SS.png"
.It Pa ~/screenshot-YYYY.MM.DD-HH.MM.SS.png
The grab.
.It Pa ~/screenshot-latest.png
Link to the newest grab.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the PNG is written.
It exits 1 when no window can be found or the grab fails.
A bad argument exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr desktop-screenshot 1 ,
.Xr gm 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
